  "id": "Compound::DB08899 - Gene::1577",
  "verbalization": "Enzalutamide is shown to interact with Cyp3a5 through multiple mechanistic pathways, primarily via its binding to Cyp2c8 and Cyp2d6, which in turn participate in aromatase activity. This pathway leads to the activation of Cyp3a5, suggesting a potential role in drug metabolism. The evidence is supported by a consistent score across three paths, indicating a plausible biological link. The shared involvement of Cyp3a5 in aromatase activity across different cytochrome P450 isoforms underscores the importance of this metabolic pathway in drug interactions. Additionally, the inclusion of Enzalutamide in the class of androgen receptor antagonists, which includes Flutamide, further supports the notion of a broader pharmacological context. The integrated evidence suggests that Enzalutamide may influence Cyp3a5 through metabolic activation, potentially affecting drug metabolism and therapeutic outcomes.",
